    {
      "title": "AI Chip Shortage: TSMC 2nm Hits 8% of Revenue in Q3 - shattered.io",
      "date": "2026-11-26",
      "source": "shattered.io",
      "url": "https://shattered.io/ai-chip-shortage-tsmc-2nm-8-percent-wafer-revenue-nov-26/",
      "summary": "AI Chip Shortage: TSMC 2nm Hits 8% of Revenue in Q3 shattered.io",
      "body": "TSMC’s 2nm process, known as N2, produced a reported 8% of the company’s wafer revenue in the third quarter of 2026, according to an OpenNash summary of TSMC’s Q3 earnings call. Reports put the second-quarter share at about 3%. That jump shows how fast the AI chip shortage is pulling the newest node into volume, and it also shows how little of that volume exists next to the orders waiting for it.\nThe question for buyers is who actually holds 2nm-class capacity today. TSMC has run N2 in high-volume manufacturing since the fourth quarter of 2025. Samsung says its SF2 process is in mass production and ramping a second generation. Intel has released a 0.9 design kit for 14A but has not confirmed a shipping product on it. Nvidia, the largest buyer of AI silicon, builds its newest Vera Rubin systems on TSMC 3nm and 5nm, according to its latest disclosures. AMD says its Venice server CPU is the first high-performance computing product to enter production on TSMC 2nm.\nLogic wafers are only one",
